workedExamples.question_text:
The graph shows a company's share price at the beginning of each month.
[tikz]
% mathsmap-diagram-colours {"version":1,"kind":"graph","base":[],"semantic":[{"name":"shareSeries","hex":"268CFF","reason":"One share-price time series and its sampled price markers"}],"reference":"Investments and Loans 1_Investment, Dividends Q8(a)-(c), lines 1647-1663 adaptation"}
\definecolor{shareSeries}{HTML}{268CFF}
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.9cm,y=2cm]
\draw[black!15,very thin,xstep=1,ystep=0.1] (0,0) grid (5,2);
\draw[->,black] (0,0)--(5.6,0) node[below right] {Month};
\draw[->,black] (0,0)--(0,2.2) node[above left] {Price (\$)};
\foreach \x/\m in {1/Jan,2/Feb,3/Mar,4/Apr,5/May} \node[below] at (\x,0) {\m};
\foreach \y/\v in {0/6.00,0.5/6.50,1/7.00,1.5/7.50,2/8.00} \node[left] at (0,\y) {\v};
\draw[very thick,shareSeries] (1,1.7)--(2,1.1)--(3,0.4)--(4,1.6)--(5,1.3);
\foreach \pt in {(1,1.7),(2,1.1),(3,0.4),(4,1.6),(5,1.3)} \fill[shareSeries] \pt circle (2pt);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
(a) Read the price in May.
(b) Find the dollar decrease from January to May.
(c) Find the percentage decrease from January to May, correct to two decimal places.

foundation.question_text:
The graph shows the monthly share price of Company A over a 6-month period.
[tikz]
% mathsmap-diagram-colours {"version":1,"kind":"graph","base":[],"semantic":[{"name":"shareSeries","hex":"268CFF","reason":"One share-price time series and its sampled price markers"}],"reference":"Stage6StandardInvestment graph interpretation; originalgraph13 adaptation"}
\definecolor{shareSeries}{HTML}{268CFF}
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.85]
\draw[black!15,very thin,xstep=1,ystep=1] (0,0) grid (6,5);
\draw[->,thick] (0,0) -- (6.5,0) node[below right,font=\small] {Month};
\draw[->,thick] (0,0) -- (0,5.5) node[above left,font=\small] {Price (\$)};
\foreach \x/\m in {1/Jan,2/Feb,3/Mar,4/Apr,5/May,6/Jun} \node[below,font=\small] at (\x,0) {\m};
\foreach \y/\v in {1/4.00,2/4.50,3/5.00,4/5.50,5/6.00} \node[left,font=\small] at (0,\y) {\v};
\node[below left,font=\small] at (0,0) {$3.50$};
\draw[very thick,shareSeries] (1,1.4) -- (2,2.6) -- (3,2.0) -- (4,3.2) -- (5,4.2) -- (6,3.6);
\foreach \pt in {(1,1.4),(2,2.6),(3,2.0),(4,3.2),(5,4.2),(6,3.6)} \fill[shareSeries] \pt circle (2.5pt);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
What was the share price at the beginning of May?

